1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,059
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,059 --> 00:00:02,059
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,059 --> 00:00:03,092
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,092 --> 00:00:04,659
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

5
00:00:04,659 --> 00:00:06,959
[Episode 11]

6
00:00:16,071 --> 00:00:17,771
Let's go together!

7
00:00:21,091 --> 00:00:25,187
I told you to stay put and learn from
your new mentor. Why look for trouble?

8
00:00:25,187 --> 00:00:27,163
Where the needle goes,
the thread must follow.

9
00:00:27,163 --> 00:00:29,459
What are you going to do without me?

10
00:00:31,799 --> 00:00:32,908
Being prepared?

11
00:00:32,908 --> 00:00:35,359
I've been ready for this for a million years!

12
00:00:35,359 --> 00:00:37,059
Keep your voice down.

13
00:00:39,723 --> 00:00:42,516
Let's go catch Kingfisher.

14
00:00:42,516 --> 00:00:43,892
Yes, sir!

15
00:00:43,892 --> 00:00:45,592
[Police]

16
00:00:47,721 --> 00:00:49,759
Mr. Lee.

17
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:50,975
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

18
00:00:50,975 --> 00:00:54,092
<i>A special task force aimed at capturing
the armed serial killer "Kingfisher"</i>

19
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:55,792
[Kingfisher Special Task Force]
<i>was launched today</i>

20
00:00:55,792 --> 00:00:58,871
<i>at the Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency.</i>

21
00:00:58,871 --> 00:01:00,610
<i>This special task force will be</i>

22
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:01,903
[Gu Tae Seok]
<i>different from those of the past.</i>

23
00:01:01,903 --> 00:01:03,487
[Head of the Kingfisher Task Force]
<i>We'll never create a task force</i>

24
00:01:03,487 --> 00:01:06,183
<i>just for show and quietly disband it later.</i>

25
00:01:06,183 --> 00:01:08,147
<i>This time, we are committed to
seeing this through to the end,</i>

26
00:01:08,147 --> 00:01:10,259
<i>and we will devote
every available resource to it.</i>

27
00:01:10,259 --> 00:01:13,492
Is this the third time they've
promised to devote every resource?

28
00:01:13,492 --> 00:01:15,567
No, it's the fourth.

29
00:01:15,567 --> 00:01:17,956
They've been creating
and disbanding these task forces

30
00:01:17,956 --> 00:01:19,283
every three or four years or so.

31
00:01:19,283 --> 00:01:21,791
What does "the end" mean this time?

32
00:01:21,791 --> 00:01:23,659
<i>That's all.</i>

33
00:01:23,659 --> 00:01:25,926
[Past Cases Under Review
with New Investigative Techniques]

34
00:01:31,775 --> 00:01:37,192
This is Inspector Yoo Mi Ran, a profiler
with the Seoul Metropolitan Police.

35
00:01:37,192 --> 00:01:39,115
[Yoo Mi Ran]

36
00:01:39,115 --> 00:01:40,487
[Kingfisher Special Task Force]
Well, you all know her, right?

37
00:01:40,487 --> 00:01:47,059
The celebrity cop who solved the 20-year-old
Oh Seong Gu serial murder case.

38
00:01:49,095 --> 00:01:53,735
I applied because I heard there was
no overtime and guaranteed time off.

39
00:01:53,735 --> 00:01:54,817
That's true, right?

40
00:01:54,817 --> 00:01:57,059
- Really?
- It's not?

41
00:01:57,059 --> 00:02:00,679
Oh, that's not good.
I might have to quit already.

42
00:02:00,679 --> 00:02:03,335
All right, now that
we've introduced ourselves,

43
00:02:03,335 --> 00:02:04,335
let's get down to business.

44
00:02:04,335 --> 00:02:06,392
[Discussion of Kingfisher Suspect Pool]

45
00:02:10,691 --> 00:02:14,192
No matter how I look at it,
I just don't understand.

46
00:02:15,479 --> 00:02:20,663
Didn't he, in a way, avenge the person
who killed his own parents?

47
00:02:20,663 --> 00:02:24,923
How can he arrest someone like that
with his own hands?

48
00:02:24,923 --> 00:02:27,091
Even if he's a police officer.

49
00:02:27,091 --> 00:02:29,867
Is avenging someone's grudge what you do?

50
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:32,826
No, it's not like that.

51
00:02:32,826 --> 00:02:36,943
Everyone just chooses their own path
for their own reasons.

52
00:02:36,943 --> 00:02:41,019
Some people can't be like us.

53
00:02:41,019 --> 00:02:43,911
And we just have to do our job.

54
00:02:43,911 --> 00:02:45,611
Right?

55
00:02:46,227 --> 00:02:47,927
Here.

56
00:02:50,343 --> 00:02:52,235
It's noon. Let's eat!

57
00:02:52,235 --> 00:02:53,935
Oh, yeah?

58
00:02:54,931 --> 00:02:58,659
So, what should we have for lunch today?

59
00:02:58,659 --> 00:03:00,935
Wow, it's already this late?

60
00:03:00,935 --> 00:03:03,143
Lunchtime!

61
00:03:03,143 --> 00:03:05,211
It's hot out. How about naengmyeon for lunch?

62
00:03:05,211 --> 00:03:06,327
Naengmyeon sounds great. Let's go.

63
00:03:06,327 --> 00:03:07,651
- Naengmyeon good.
- Come on, Manager Go, let's go.

64
00:03:07,651 --> 00:03:08,700
Alright.

65
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,892
I want naengmyeon in chilled broth.

66
00:03:13,999 --> 00:03:17,119
I wonder if Manager Tae Min
is going to grab something quick again.

67
00:03:17,119 --> 00:03:20,139
Oh, I don't know how
he can eat in places like that.

68
00:03:20,139 --> 00:03:23,099
Don't worry. He'll be eating properly
for the time being.

69
00:03:23,099 --> 00:03:25,291
Huh? For the time being?

70
00:03:25,291 --> 00:03:26,991
Why?

71
00:04:16,227 --> 00:04:18,895
[Discussion of Kingfisher Suspect Pool]
Kingfisher is a methodical killer

72
00:04:18,895 --> 00:04:22,207
who operates with a clear motive
and objective.

73
00:04:22,207 --> 00:04:26,687
His weapon of choice is a sniper rifle,
hard for civilians to obtain.

74
00:04:26,687 --> 00:04:29,946
Given the circumstances, we should
probably start from the fact that

75
00:04:29,946 --> 00:04:31,635
he's physically very capable, right?

76
00:04:31,635 --> 00:04:34,926
Special forces background
seems like the closest fit, doesn't it?

77
00:04:34,926 --> 00:04:37,559
I've already looked into that sector.

78
00:04:37,559 --> 00:04:39,725
I screened 400 individuals
who served in military special forces

79
00:04:39,725 --> 00:04:42,399
before Kingfisher first appeared in 2010,

80
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:44,866
focusing on those
with exceptional marksmanship,

81
00:04:44,866 --> 00:04:46,559
and investigated them one by one.

82
00:04:46,559 --> 00:04:48,628
I found nothing.

83
00:04:48,628 --> 00:04:52,092
You were practically
looking for a needle in a haystack.

84
00:04:53,271 --> 00:04:58,759
So all 400 special forces veterans
were adult Korean men?

85
00:04:59,859 --> 00:05:03,143
Well, yes, naturally...

86
00:05:03,143 --> 00:05:08,047
So are you saying Kingfisher
could be a woman or even a minor?

87
00:05:08,047 --> 00:05:09,792
What is this, a movie?

88
00:05:12,483 --> 00:05:14,963
We shouldn't be constrained by the assumption

89
00:05:14,963 --> 00:05:16,615
that Kingfisher is an adult Korean male.

90
00:05:16,615 --> 00:05:18,895
We need to keep every possibility open.

91
00:05:18,895 --> 00:05:23,507
Gender, age, nationality, and so on.

92
00:05:23,507 --> 00:05:25,599
<i>Kingfisher is...</i>

93
00:05:25,599 --> 00:05:27,692
a tall...

94
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:33,492
well-built young man.

95
00:05:34,483 --> 00:05:38,255
And there's one more thing
we need to pay attention to.

96
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:40,471
It's the cooling-off periods.

97
00:05:40,471 --> 00:05:43,626
You mean the Haegong-dong Gosiwon case?

98
00:05:43,626 --> 00:05:46,003
Well, you're right.

99
00:05:46,003 --> 00:05:49,059
There was a four-year gap
in his activity after that.

100
00:05:49,059 --> 00:05:53,123
A serial killer's hiatus is usually
explained in one of two ways.

101
00:05:53,123 --> 00:05:56,883
One is external control, like restrictions
from arrest or incarceration.

102
00:05:56,883 --> 00:05:59,359
The other is an internal load state.

103
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:05,192
When the desire is temporarily satisfied,
the impulse subsides.

104
00:06:06,007 --> 00:06:10,167
But I believe Kingfisher is different.

105
00:06:10,167 --> 00:06:11,195
Why?

106
00:06:11,195 --> 00:06:14,959
Because Kingfisher isn't

107
00:06:15,675 --> 00:06:17,375
an ordinary psychopath.

108
00:06:18,319 --> 00:06:20,523
You're suggesting there
may have been some change

109
00:06:20,523 --> 00:06:23,659
in his state of mind or
his surrounding circumstances?

110
00:06:23,659 --> 00:06:24,659
Exactly.

111
00:06:24,659 --> 00:06:27,315
[Analysis of Cooling-Off Periods]

112
00:06:27,315 --> 00:06:29,051
There was another one
besides Haegong-dong, right?

113
00:06:29,051 --> 00:06:30,180
[The two gaps may provide clues]
Eight years ago,

114
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,231
[to Kingfisher's true identity]
the so-called "World Cup incident"

115
00:06:32,231 --> 00:06:34,723
was followed by a nine-month gap.

116
00:06:34,723 --> 00:06:37,779
Given that his previous crime intervals
were no more than two months,

117
00:06:37,779 --> 00:06:41,239
it's clearly... a significant figure.

118
00:06:41,239 --> 00:06:45,795
So, I believe these two gaps,
one long and one short,

119
00:06:45,795 --> 00:06:51,126
may provide clues to
Kingfisher's true identity.

120
00:06:52,091 --> 00:06:56,023
Okay, just as Ms. Yoo suggested,
let's keep open the possibility that

121
00:06:56,023 --> 00:06:57,807
Kingfisher could be a woman or even a minor,

122
00:06:57,807 --> 00:06:59,571
and look more closely at the commonalities

123
00:06:59,571 --> 00:07:01,751
between the World Cup and Haegong-dong cases.

124
00:07:01,751 --> 00:07:03,807
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, understood.

125
00:07:03,807 --> 00:07:05,526
- Yes.
- Understood.

126
00:07:07,655 --> 00:07:09,513
<i>The World Cup case and the Haegong-dong case.</i>

127
00:07:09,513 --> 00:07:12,003
You were there for both major incidents.

128
00:07:12,003 --> 00:07:13,497
The odds of that are practically impossible.

129
00:07:13,497 --> 00:07:16,092
I'm a reporter, you punk!

130
00:07:30,103 --> 00:07:31,931
<i>I heard your reporter friend woke up.</i>

131
00:07:31,931 --> 00:07:32,975
That's a relief.

132
00:07:32,975 --> 00:07:35,367
Oh, he barely made it back
from the brink of death.

133
00:07:35,367 --> 00:07:39,259
Oh, did he find his savior? The person
who called an ambulance for him.

134
00:07:39,259 --> 00:07:40,543
Oh, that woman?

135
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:43,992
She made the call from my friend's phone,
so it's difficult to identify her.

136
00:07:47,831 --> 00:07:52,692
But apparently that's the building
where Kingfisher took the shot,

137
00:07:52,692 --> 00:07:54,475
and the timing roughly lines up too.

138
00:07:54,475 --> 00:08:00,092
I was wondering if Kingfisher
might have made the call.

139
00:08:00,871 --> 00:08:05,123
Killed someone from above
and saved a life on the way down?

140
00:08:05,123 --> 00:08:07,083
And a woman, no less?

141
00:08:07,083 --> 00:08:08,426
Yes.

142
00:08:08,426 --> 00:08:10,059
Oh, for God's sake.

143
00:08:10,059 --> 00:08:11,529
Stop chasing wild theories
about someone else's case

144
00:08:11,529 --> 00:08:13,692
and focus on your own case, punk.

145
00:08:26,026 --> 00:08:28,092
[City Mania Hotel Incident]

146
00:08:35,126 --> 00:08:37,892
[Witness Interview Report]

147
00:08:39,839 --> 00:08:41,571
<i>Looking back later,</i>

148
00:08:41,571 --> 00:08:44,231
[Under Investigation]
all the security cameras were broken.

149
00:08:44,231 --> 00:08:46,067
I didn't know while I was on duty.

150
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,459
The monitors appeared to be working normally.

151
00:08:48,459 --> 00:08:50,819
Was there absolutely
no one else in the building?

152
00:08:50,819 --> 00:08:52,495
Like the cleaning crew?

153
00:08:52,495 --> 00:08:57,183
There were no employees
working late that day.

154
00:08:57,183 --> 00:08:59,251
<i>And the cleaning crew left early.</i>

155
00:08:59,251 --> 00:09:01,959
<i>They left before the crowds
started coming in.</i>

156
00:09:01,959 --> 00:09:04,539
<i>It wasn't an employee or a cleaner.</i>

157
00:09:04,539 --> 00:09:06,359
<i>Then who was it?</i>

158
00:09:06,359 --> 00:09:09,099
<i>Who reported Tae Seong?</i>

159
00:09:09,099 --> 00:09:12,092
Oh, Kwon Se Ah is always busy.

160
00:09:18,695 --> 00:09:19,903
What are you looking for?

161
00:09:19,903 --> 00:09:21,126
It's not here...

162
00:09:21,126 --> 00:09:23,247
The records related to Tae Seong's case...

163
00:09:23,247 --> 00:09:25,303
Tae Seong?

164
00:09:25,303 --> 00:09:26,845
Oh, you mean the case where he was mugged

165
00:09:26,845 --> 00:09:29,071
while chasing a pickpocket
during the World Cup?

166
00:09:29,071 --> 00:09:32,343
Why is that in there?
It wasn't even a Kingfisher case.

167
00:09:32,343 --> 00:09:35,319
Could those two cases be unrelated?

168
00:09:35,319 --> 00:09:37,026
Or what?

169
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:46,559
Where are you going?

170
00:09:46,559 --> 00:09:47,743
The prison.

171
00:09:47,743 --> 00:09:48,867
Follow me if you want.

172
00:09:48,867 --> 00:09:50,227
What? Why a prison?

173
00:09:50,227 --> 00:09:51,303
Who is there?

174
00:09:51,303 --> 00:09:53,326
Someone we excluded
from the investigation back then.

175
00:09:53,326 --> 00:09:55,867
So who is that? Huh?

176
00:10:09,507 --> 00:10:10,507
[Green Sky Welfare Center]

177
00:10:10,507 --> 00:10:11,659
<i>Her grandson?</i>

178
00:10:11,659 --> 00:10:13,826
Oh, the boy who spoke strangely
and barely talked?

179
00:10:13,826 --> 00:10:17,707
Yeah. He'd been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

180
00:10:17,707 --> 00:10:19,771
Do you happen to know where he is now?

181
00:10:19,771 --> 00:10:21,892
Didn't he end up in some kind of institution?

182
00:10:21,892 --> 00:10:26,792
<i>Yeah. There was no one to take care of him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.</i>

183
00:10:30,951 --> 00:10:32,319
You said you came to see Cheol, right?

184
00:10:32,319 --> 00:10:34,379
Yes.

185
00:10:34,379 --> 00:10:37,059
That's him over there.

186
00:10:43,543 --> 00:10:45,152
When he first came here,

187
00:10:45,152 --> 00:10:48,503
he struggled to express himself
and interact with others,

188
00:10:48,503 --> 00:10:50,587
but he's much brighter now.

189
00:10:50,587 --> 00:10:52,219
That's good to hear.

190
00:10:52,219 --> 00:10:55,263
He seems to like drawing.

191
00:10:55,263 --> 00:10:57,911
A sponsor sends him flowers every week,

192
00:10:57,911 --> 00:11:00,667
and on those days he always
draws flowers like that.

193
00:11:00,667 --> 00:11:02,007
A sponsor?

194
00:11:02,007 --> 00:11:07,692
There's an anonymous sponsor who funds
various treatment programs for Cheol.

195
00:11:08,979 --> 00:11:11,659
What is their relationship to the child?

196
00:11:11,659 --> 00:11:14,692
Well, I'm not sure about that.

197
00:11:17,295 --> 00:11:21,983
If you don't mind, could I meet them?

198
00:11:21,983 --> 00:11:26,292
I'm afraid that's not possible.
They don't want anyone to know who they are.

199
00:11:33,059 --> 00:11:39,063
When sending flowers,
they always add a flower language card.

200
00:11:39,063 --> 00:11:43,583
The very first time, there was
also a separate message card.

201
00:11:43,583 --> 00:11:46,835
"I hope you find your own beautiful view."

202
00:11:46,835 --> 00:11:48,992
That was all it said.

203
00:11:53,592 --> 00:11:55,987
What did you just say?

204
00:11:55,987 --> 00:11:58,751
- Excuse me?
- The message on the first card they sent.

205
00:11:58,751 --> 00:12:02,792
"I hope you find your own
beautiful view." That one?

206
00:12:04,259 --> 00:12:06,459
<i>I think that's the power of a beautiful view.</i>

207
00:12:06,459 --> 00:12:08,183
My own little views that give me energy

208
00:12:08,183 --> 00:12:12,167
when I'm tired and help me
get moving again when I stop.

209
00:12:12,167 --> 00:12:15,859
Have you ever had a beautiful moment
like that in your life, Bo Na?

210
00:12:21,099 --> 00:12:23,295
Oh, I'm sorry.

211
00:12:23,295 --> 00:12:25,659
That's a beautiful thing to say.

212
00:12:26,603 --> 00:12:30,459
They must have a very romantic,
almost girlish sensibility.

213
00:12:30,459 --> 00:12:31,559
I guess so.

214
00:12:31,559 --> 00:12:35,292
But their way of talking
is so blunt, like a guy.

215
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:52,792
[Ok's Flower Shop]

216
00:12:56,851 --> 00:13:00,623
So that pickpocket wasn't caught
until a full year later.

217
00:13:00,623 --> 00:13:02,931
Huh? But why is he still in here?

218
00:13:02,931 --> 00:13:06,192
Because he was charged with
aggravated assault and fleeing.

219
00:13:12,259 --> 00:13:15,859
Prison food must suit you well.
You look healthy.

220
00:13:20,575 --> 00:13:22,451
It's been a while.

221
00:13:22,451 --> 00:13:24,919
So, why are you here now,
after all this time?

222
00:13:24,919 --> 00:13:27,259
Here to grab me by the collar again?

223
00:13:30,283 --> 00:13:32,479
Your friend is safe and sound, huh?

224
00:13:32,479 --> 00:13:34,883
Yeah, he's doing fine.

225
00:13:34,883 --> 00:13:36,375
I just came to ask you something.

226
00:13:36,375 --> 00:13:38,067
That day you mugged him.

227
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:41,759
I told you everything about the day.
What else do you want?

228
00:13:45,292 --> 00:13:47,507
Your friend kept chasing me,

229
00:13:47,507 --> 00:13:50,526
so I hit him with a fire extinguisher
to knock him out...

230
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:52,711
But I hit him too hard.

231
00:13:52,711 --> 00:13:55,159
I know all that. What happens next?

232
00:13:55,159 --> 00:13:56,543
After you hit him.

233
00:13:56,543 --> 00:13:58,535
So, I ran outside.

234
00:13:58,535 --> 00:14:00,007
You left through the first-floor lobby?

235
00:14:00,007 --> 00:14:02,123
Of course, I left through
the first floor. Where else?

236
00:14:02,123 --> 00:14:05,547
Did you see anyone while you were
making your way out?

237
00:14:05,547 --> 00:14:07,523
See what?

238
00:14:07,523 --> 00:14:09,692
It was dark and completely empty.

239
00:14:11,675 --> 00:14:13,343
Wait.

240
00:14:13,343 --> 00:14:17,526
Come to think of it,
there may have been someone.

241
00:14:18,151 --> 00:14:20,383
There was?

242
00:14:20,383 --> 00:14:21,395
Who?

243
00:14:21,395 --> 00:14:24,095
Oh, but can I say I saw someone?

244
00:14:24,095 --> 00:14:25,567
It wasn't actually inside the building.

245
00:14:25,567 --> 00:14:29,459
Inside or outside the building, who was it?

246
00:14:29,459 --> 00:14:31,326
A woman.

247
00:14:40,292 --> 00:14:42,159
[King Tower]

248
00:14:43,555 --> 00:14:48,226
<i>At the time Tae Seong entered the King Tower
building chasing the pickpocket,</i>

249
00:14:49,159 --> 00:14:53,292
<i>Kingfisher was on the roof of that building.</i>

250
00:15:14,059 --> 00:15:17,163
<i>The victim was on the phone
with a friend at a hotel across the street.</i>

251
00:15:17,163 --> 00:15:19,757
- <i>During the call,</i>
- So what? Hello?

252
00:15:19,757 --> 00:15:22,392
<i>South Korea scored their first goal,</i>

253
00:15:23,243 --> 00:15:25,627
<i>and moments later,
he was shot dead by a sniper.</i>

254
00:15:25,627 --> 00:15:28,826
<i>It was 11:02 PM.</i>

255
00:15:33,067 --> 00:15:37,059
<i>It would have taken just over
a minute to walk quickly from the rooftop</i>

256
00:15:37,059 --> 00:15:39,083
<i>down to the fifth floor.</i>

257
00:15:39,083 --> 00:15:43,026
<i>If she found Tae Seong
collapsed here at that time...</i>

258
00:15:45,807 --> 00:15:51,195
The records show the emergency call
came in at 11:07 PM.

259
00:15:51,195 --> 00:15:54,723
It was a long time ago,
but do you remember the caller's voice?

260
00:15:54,723 --> 00:15:56,771
Their way of speaking or accent?

261
00:15:56,771 --> 00:15:59,092
Well, it was a long time ago...

262
00:15:59,092 --> 00:16:02,507
I just remember that she sounded
like a young woman.

263
00:16:02,507 --> 00:16:06,719
I think she briefly stated what happened
and hung up right away.

264
00:16:06,719 --> 00:16:10,759
Oh, I remember someone shouting nearby
just before the call came in.

265
00:16:10,759 --> 00:16:13,671
I think Korea had just scored
and taken the lead?

266
00:16:13,671 --> 00:16:18,307
<i>Korea scored its second goal at 11:06 PM.</i>

267
00:16:18,307 --> 00:16:21,592
<i>The ambulance call
came in immediately afterward.</i>

268
00:16:28,626 --> 00:16:31,326
[Gate 3]

269
00:16:35,126 --> 00:16:39,392
If we open the first-floor restroom
to the public, it gets insanely dirty.

270
00:16:39,392 --> 00:16:44,411
<i>So the owner ordered us to lock
all the doors and said no one gets in.</i>

271
00:16:44,411 --> 00:16:50,559
But then some lunatic opened one of
the first-floor doors without me knowing.

272
00:17:02,579 --> 00:17:06,692
<i>It took roughly two minutes to get
from the fifth-floor stairs to outside.</i>

273
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:12,359
<i>And right here,
the pickpocket said he saw a woman.</i>

274
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:14,059
<i>A woman?</i>

275
00:17:14,691 --> 00:17:17,467
- Are you sure?
- I told you, yes.

276
00:17:17,467 --> 00:17:20,431
It's not like I can't tell
a man from a woman.

277
00:17:20,431 --> 00:17:23,499
[Parking Lot Entrance]
<i>It was my first time hitting someone,</i>

278
00:17:23,499 --> 00:17:25,092
<i>so I was nervous about what would happen</i>

279
00:17:25,092 --> 00:17:28,831
<i>and was hanging around nearby
to keep an eye on things.</i>

280
00:17:28,831 --> 00:17:31,963
<i>Then I saw a woman come out of the building.</i>

281
00:17:31,963 --> 00:17:35,959
<i>It was too dark to see her face.
I only saw her from behind.</i>

282
00:17:35,959 --> 00:17:42,119
She was wearing a red T-shirt
and some kind of pointed headband.

283
00:17:42,119 --> 00:17:45,959
I figured the Red Devil, a World Cup fan,
had just been to the bathroom.

284
00:17:45,959 --> 00:17:47,892
The Red Devil?

285
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:50,392
Was she alone?

286
00:17:50,392 --> 00:17:52,111
Yes, she was alone.

287
00:17:52,111 --> 00:17:55,992
Do you remember anything else?
Like her build or hairstyle.

288
00:17:55,992 --> 00:17:58,126
She was pretty tall...

289
00:17:58,927 --> 00:18:01,392
and seemed slender.

290
00:18:02,027 --> 00:18:03,975
I think she had short hair.

291
00:18:03,975 --> 00:18:06,059
[Headband, Red Devil]
Short hair...

292
00:18:06,059 --> 00:18:07,303
No, maybe it was tied back?

293
00:18:07,303 --> 00:18:10,030
Was she carrying or wearing anything else?

294
00:18:10,030 --> 00:18:14,991
Oh, right. She had a big bag
slung over her shoulder.

295
00:18:14,991 --> 00:18:18,459
About this big?

296
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:20,831
She was tall...

297
00:18:20,831 --> 00:18:22,126
What time did you see her?

298
00:18:22,126 --> 00:18:24,853
Come on, how would I remember that?

299
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:29,392
Oh, but when she came out,
I think Korea scored a goal or something.

300
00:18:29,392 --> 00:18:32,559
Everyone was cheering like crazy

301
00:18:32,559 --> 00:18:34,355
<i>and making a huge commotion.</i>

302
00:18:34,355 --> 00:18:37,667
<i>Around 11:10 PM, give or take.</i>

303
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:40,292
<i>Given the route and timing,</i>

304
00:18:40,292 --> 00:18:43,995
<i>it's highly likely that
the woman who reported Tae Seong</i>

305
00:18:43,995 --> 00:18:46,292
<i>and the woman seen by the pickpocket
were the same person.</i>

306
00:18:47,031 --> 00:18:48,839
<i>Then...</i>

307
00:18:48,839 --> 00:18:53,226
Kingfisher is a tall,

308
00:18:53,226 --> 00:18:56,959
<i>well-built young man.</i>

309
00:19:05,559 --> 00:19:09,592
[Mr. Tiger]

310
00:19:14,763 --> 00:19:16,692
<i>Why aren't you answering again?</i>

311
00:19:19,267 --> 00:19:20,967
<i>Busy.</i>

312
00:19:21,911 --> 00:19:23,626
<i>Call me when you're free.</i>

313
00:19:24,487 --> 00:19:26,187
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

314
00:19:28,059 --> 00:19:29,140
[- What are you doing tonight?
- Busy.]

315
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:30,192
[- What are you up to this weekend?
- Busy.]

316
00:19:30,192 --> 00:19:32,259
[- Gaming cafe today? What are you doing?
- Busy.]

317
00:19:35,947 --> 00:19:38,092
I usually just come here to deliver chicken.

318
00:19:38,092 --> 00:19:40,526
This is the first time I've come here
for something like this.

319
00:19:40,526 --> 00:19:45,427
I somehow ended up helping catch
criminals too. It's a pretty strange feeling.

320
00:19:45,427 --> 00:19:47,543
You deliver chicken?

321
00:19:47,543 --> 00:19:51,159
Seong Hun orders chicken
from our place all the time.

322
00:19:51,159 --> 00:19:54,192
Even though I keep telling him
to order from somewhere nearby,

323
00:19:54,192 --> 00:19:57,759
he says there aren't
any chicken places around here.

324
00:19:57,759 --> 00:20:01,359
How do you know him?

325
00:20:02,292 --> 00:20:04,147
We met at a judo gym in elementary school.

326
00:20:04,147 --> 00:20:06,792
On his first day, he underestimated me
and picked a fight,

327
00:20:06,792 --> 00:20:08,675
so I threw him in one move.

328
00:20:08,675 --> 00:20:11,543
I guess he was embarrassed,
so he asked me to keep it a secret.

329
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,655
So I suggested we become friends instead.

330
00:20:13,655 --> 00:20:16,659
He's actually two years older than me.

331
00:20:18,051 --> 00:20:19,751
Se Ah.

332
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:25,347
Shall we meet again?

333
00:20:25,347 --> 00:20:27,092
You startled me.

334
00:20:28,243 --> 00:20:30,371
Why?

335
00:20:30,371 --> 00:20:33,867
I've started wanting to know
what kind of person you are.

336
00:20:33,867 --> 00:20:35,995
Really?

337
00:20:35,995 --> 00:20:38,955
Yes, I'd love to! Let's meet!

338
00:20:38,955 --> 00:20:41,992
Next time, just the two of us.

339
00:20:43,391 --> 00:20:45,959
Since he seems to have feelings for you.

340
00:20:51,791 --> 00:20:55,339
No way! That's ridiculous.

341
00:20:55,339 --> 00:20:57,364
We've known each other long enough

342
00:20:57,364 --> 00:20:59,459
to have seen each other
at our best and worst.

343
00:20:59,459 --> 00:21:02,063
Oh, come on. No, no.

344
00:21:02,063 --> 00:21:04,259
Come on, no chance!

345
00:21:07,619 --> 00:21:09,892
Oh, dear. I'm home from school.

346
00:21:09,892 --> 00:21:11,592
You're back?

347
00:21:13,403 --> 00:21:15,675
Why's Mom so happy today?

348
00:21:15,675 --> 00:21:16,675
Oh, so happy!

349
00:21:16,675 --> 00:21:19,092
Today's the day she gets
her savings out. Five years' worth.

350
00:21:19,092 --> 00:21:21,559
Wow, today's the day?

351
00:21:21,559 --> 00:21:24,919
No wonder you're happy with
a big chunk of money coming in.

352
00:21:24,919 --> 00:21:26,526
What, is she paying off the loan?

353
00:21:26,526 --> 00:21:28,087
She said she was
planning to redo the kitchen.

354
00:21:28,087 --> 00:21:30,043
The fryer is pretty old.

355
00:21:30,043 --> 00:21:32,859
Hey, this is the last delivery, isn't it?

356
00:21:32,859 --> 00:21:34,227
Yeah, the last one.

357
00:21:34,227 --> 00:21:36,779
Okay, I'll do it, and...

358
00:21:36,779 --> 00:21:37,815
What time is it now?

359
00:21:37,815 --> 00:21:42,639
Oh, my, I'll stop by the bank,
go grocery shopping, and head straight home.

360
00:21:42,639 --> 00:21:46,392
So come home later.
Let's wrap up early today.

361
00:21:46,392 --> 00:21:47,392
Oh, dear.

362
00:21:47,392 --> 00:21:49,535
What? Are we having
something delicious today?

363
00:21:49,535 --> 00:21:50,967
Then I'll have beef.

364
00:21:50,967 --> 00:21:53,415
Beef?

365
00:21:53,415 --> 00:21:55,723
- Sure, let's have it.
- Wow!

366
00:21:55,723 --> 00:21:56,840
Goodness.

367
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:59,659
Tell Tae Seong's family to come if they can.

368
00:22:01,179 --> 00:22:02,851
Mom, buy lots of meat.

369
00:22:02,851 --> 00:22:05,526
- Korean beef!
- See you later.

370
00:22:07,563 --> 00:22:10,326
Looks like she's planning to
apologize with beef.

371
00:22:11,159 --> 00:22:13,999
Hey, you go handle this one.
Bunhong Apartments.

372
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:17,423
Come on, I told you to call a courier!

373
00:22:17,423 --> 00:22:19,643
Hey, Seong Hun stopped by yesterday.

374
00:22:19,643 --> 00:22:21,283
Huh? What? Why?

375
00:22:21,283 --> 00:22:23,047
Why else? He came to buy chicken.

376
00:22:23,047 --> 00:22:25,974
He asked if something happened because
he hasn't been able to reach you lately.

377
00:22:25,974 --> 00:22:27,092
Did you two have a fight?

378
00:22:27,092 --> 00:22:29,939
Come on, we're not kids.

379
00:22:29,939 --> 00:22:32,547
Where? Bunhong Apartments? I'm going!

380
00:22:32,547 --> 00:22:34,575
Hey, you need the building and unit number!

381
00:22:34,575 --> 00:22:36,892
Building 108, Unit 504!

382
00:22:43,323 --> 00:22:44,959
Oh.

383
00:22:44,959 --> 00:22:45,959
Hello?

384
00:22:45,959 --> 00:22:48,300
<i>Hello, is this Ms. Ok Seon Ja?</i>

385
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,631
Yes. Who is this?

386
00:22:49,631 --> 00:22:52,618
<i>I'm Manager Kim Mi So
from the Korea Inclusive Finance Agency,</i>

387
00:22:52,618 --> 00:22:54,039
<i>a government-affiliated institution.</i>

388
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:58,554
<i>I'm calling because you've been
selected for a low-interest loan program.</i>

389
00:22:58,554 --> 00:23:02,939
Me? Why? I don't need a loan.

390
00:23:02,939 --> 00:23:04,692
<i>It's a loan program designed for</i>

391
00:23:04,692 --> 00:23:09,283
<i>self-employed business owners
with interest rates around 0.8%.</i>

392
00:23:09,283 --> 00:23:11,135
0.8%?

393
00:23:11,135 --> 00:23:13,059
<i>Yes, according to our records,</i>

394
00:23:13,059 --> 00:23:16,791
<i>you previously took out a loan
with Haneop Bank.</i>

395
00:23:16,791 --> 00:23:20,007
Oh, yes. I do. That was...

396
00:23:20,007 --> 00:23:22,039
I think it was around 4.2%?

397
00:23:22,039 --> 00:23:23,964
<i>Our rates are much lower,</i>

398
00:23:23,964 --> 00:23:26,692
<i>so a lot of people move their loans here
to save on interest.</i>

399
00:23:26,692 --> 00:23:29,192
<i>Some even save a million won a month.</i>

400
00:23:29,192 --> 00:23:30,503
As much as a million won?

401
00:23:30,503 --> 00:23:33,091
<i>Yes, a million won.</i>

402
00:23:33,091 --> 00:23:34,939
Oh, my, what?

403
00:23:34,939 --> 00:23:36,043
Wow, that's great.

404
00:23:36,043 --> 00:23:38,148
<i>But there's just one condition.</i>

405
00:23:38,148 --> 00:23:42,492
<i>You have to pay off your
existing loan first to use ours.</i>

406
00:23:42,492 --> 00:23:45,326
<i>Would you be interested?</i>

407
00:23:45,326 --> 00:23:47,692
Well, I'm not sure...

408
00:23:47,692 --> 00:23:50,159
I'll check with the kids first.

409
00:23:50,159 --> 00:23:53,659
<i>But the deadline is today,
so if you're not interested,</i>

410
00:23:53,659 --> 00:23:55,719
<i>I need to contact the next person right away.</i>

411
00:23:55,719 --> 00:23:59,159
No, wait.

412
00:24:01,359 --> 00:24:04,399
I'll do it! What do I need to do?

413
00:24:04,399 --> 00:24:08,031
<i>You need to repay the loan by today.
Can you pay back the loan today?</i>

414
00:24:08,031 --> 00:24:09,759
What?

415
00:24:11,175 --> 00:24:14,323
I happen to have the money.

416
00:24:14,323 --> 00:24:16,760
But the bank is closed right now.

417
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:21,526
<i>Then I'll connect you with a Haneop Bank
branch partnered with our agency.</i>

418
00:24:24,295 --> 00:24:25,995
[Financial Fraud Prevention
Questionnaire Page, No]

419
00:24:42,744 --> 00:24:44,859
Oh, let's go.

420
00:24:44,859 --> 00:24:46,759
Yeah. Honey, did you hear?

421
00:24:46,759 --> 00:24:49,723
Mom wants to have a beef feast.
When are you done?

422
00:24:49,723 --> 00:24:53,123
I'm out reporting, but it shouldn't
take long. I'll come as soon as I'm done.

423
00:24:53,123 --> 00:24:55,126
<i>Okay, see you later.</i>

424
00:25:10,192 --> 00:25:11,267
[Ok's Flower Shop]

425
00:25:11,267 --> 00:25:13,826
- Then I'll get going.
- Thank you.

426
00:25:26,992 --> 00:25:29,459
[Ok's Flower Shop]

427
00:25:30,359 --> 00:25:32,755
[Ok's Flower Shop]

428
00:25:32,755 --> 00:25:35,519
So this place has been here all along?

429
00:25:35,519 --> 00:25:36,685
Welcome!

430
00:25:36,685 --> 00:25:38,385
Hello.

431
00:25:40,547 --> 00:25:43,447
I didn't know there was such a pretty
flower shop in our neighborhood.

432
00:25:43,447 --> 00:25:46,579
Oh, you live nearby.

433
00:25:46,579 --> 00:25:49,819
People who mostly drive around
could easily miss it.

434
00:25:49,819 --> 00:25:53,543
Right. Men don't usually
pay much attention to flowers.

435
00:25:53,543 --> 00:25:56,699
So I guess most of your customers
are women who live nearby.

436
00:25:56,699 --> 00:25:57,792
Why?

437
00:25:57,792 --> 00:26:02,835
Lots of men come in to buy flowers
for their wives or girlfriends.

438
00:26:02,835 --> 00:26:04,292
I see.

439
00:26:04,292 --> 00:26:06,459
- Can I look around...
- Yes.

440
00:26:16,091 --> 00:26:19,426
Are you looking for a particular flower?

441
00:26:20,515 --> 00:26:23,125
What's the meaning of this flower?

442
00:26:23,125 --> 00:26:24,327
Sunflowers?

443
00:26:24,327 --> 00:26:27,326
They stand for hope, positivity, and support.

444
00:26:27,326 --> 00:26:31,681
People often give them
as congratulatory gifts or get-well gifts.

445
00:26:31,681 --> 00:26:33,775
It also means purifying
the dark energy in the home

446
00:26:33,775 --> 00:26:37,127
and filling it with bright, positive energy.

447
00:26:37,127 --> 00:26:39,159
I see. That's what it means.

448
00:26:41,178 --> 00:26:42,878
Well...

449
00:26:44,791 --> 00:26:49,526
Actually, I came to ask you something.

450
00:26:49,526 --> 00:26:52,003
[Not Today Reporter, Kwon Tae Seong]

451
00:26:52,003 --> 00:26:56,659
Could you tell me anything about the person
who sends flowers to Yeon Cheol?

452
00:26:56,659 --> 00:26:58,775
Yeon Cheol...

453
00:26:58,775 --> 00:27:02,118
- Oh, the kid at the welfare center?
- Yes.

454
00:27:02,118 --> 00:27:05,726
Well, I just take the orders
and deliver the flowers.

455
00:27:07,372 --> 00:27:09,043
What about the flower meanings?

456
00:27:09,043 --> 00:27:12,307
I heard they send a card
explaining them every time.

457
00:27:12,307 --> 00:27:13,595
That was me.

458
00:27:13,595 --> 00:27:15,991
They never gave me
a specific message to pass along,

459
00:27:15,991 --> 00:27:18,959
and sending flowers
with nothing at all felt a little empty.

460
00:27:19,783 --> 00:27:23,007
But one of the staff members remembered
what was written on the first card.

461
00:27:23,007 --> 00:27:24,471
Then, could that have been...

462
00:27:24,471 --> 00:27:27,935
The first card...
I suppose it was probably that.

463
00:27:27,935 --> 00:27:30,219
Do you remember what you wrote?

464
00:27:30,219 --> 00:27:33,392
Well, what was it again?

465
00:27:34,071 --> 00:27:37,323
<i>"I hope you find your own beautiful view."</i>

466
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:39,087
<i>That was all it said.</i>

467
00:27:39,087 --> 00:27:42,747
"I hope you always smile
as brightly as a flower."

468
00:27:42,747 --> 00:27:45,363
Oh, right. That's what I wrote.

469
00:27:45,363 --> 00:27:48,326
Since they were for a child, after all.

470
00:27:55,795 --> 00:27:57,495
Oh, hello.

471
00:27:59,127 --> 00:28:03,426
I'm Assistant Manager Kwon Dong Hun
from Haneop Bank's Gwanghwamun branch.

472
00:28:03,426 --> 00:28:05,131
[Assistant Manager Kwon Dong Hun]

473
00:28:05,131 --> 00:28:07,579
But how am I supposed to know you're really

474
00:28:07,579 --> 00:28:09,495
with the bank from just a business card?

475
00:28:09,495 --> 00:28:12,235
It's just that the world is
so full of scams these days.

476
00:28:12,235 --> 00:28:14,207
Of course, completely understandable.

477
00:28:14,207 --> 00:28:19,451
Alright, here's my bank ID card.

478
00:28:19,451 --> 00:28:23,847
- These are the loan repayment documents.
- Oh, oh... Yes.

479
00:28:23,847 --> 00:28:27,459
Take your time reading them,
and then sign here.

480
00:28:28,867 --> 00:28:30,595
[Loan Repayment]
Oh, right. This is right.

481
00:28:30,595 --> 00:28:36,292
- Oh, okay, just a moment.
- Sure, take your time.

482
00:28:43,999 --> 00:28:46,763
- I've signed this part.
- Oh, yes.

483
00:28:46,763 --> 00:28:48,463
By the way...

484
00:28:49,323 --> 00:28:52,331
this will pay off my loan, right?

485
00:28:52,331 --> 00:28:53,459
Of course.

486
00:28:53,459 --> 00:28:57,091
You called the bank yourself, after all.

487
00:28:57,091 --> 00:28:59,091
Alright, then...

488
00:28:59,091 --> 00:29:00,791
Wait...

489
00:29:01,491 --> 00:29:03,192
Well...

490
00:29:03,892 --> 00:29:06,126
Well, Ma'am.

491
00:29:06,126 --> 00:29:10,759
My team leader is actually
waiting for me and can't leave work yet.

492
00:29:11,631 --> 00:29:15,559
Oh, I'm so sorry.

493
00:29:15,559 --> 00:29:18,526
I'm so sorry. You're so busy,
couldn't even leave work,

494
00:29:18,526 --> 00:29:20,959
and still came all the way
to my home. Thank you.

495
00:29:20,959 --> 00:29:23,223
Oh, we're the ones who should thank you.

496
00:29:23,223 --> 00:29:25,608
- I'll make sure your money
- Yeah.

497
00:29:25,608 --> 00:29:27,695
gets safely transferred.

498
00:29:27,695 --> 00:29:31,759
Okay. Please take good care of it.

499
00:29:31,759 --> 00:29:32,992
- Yes.
- Please go inside.

500
00:29:32,992 --> 00:29:35,592
- Yes...
- Don't worry about a thing.

501
00:29:35,592 --> 00:29:36,892
Keep the money safe.

502
00:29:36,892 --> 00:29:38,107
- Go inside.
- Yes.

503
00:29:38,107 --> 00:29:40,159
- Call us again if you need anything.
- Okay.

504
00:29:49,359 --> 00:29:51,811
[Boss]

505
00:29:51,811 --> 00:29:54,631
Darn it, the old lady was so suspicious.

506
00:29:54,631 --> 00:29:57,319
Does she really think
that makes her look smart?

507
00:29:57,319 --> 00:29:59,711
Sure, I made it back safe and sound.

508
00:29:59,711 --> 00:30:02,592
But the commission is 10%, right?

509
00:30:04,135 --> 00:30:06,892
Yes. I'll meet you there.

510
00:30:08,726 --> 00:30:11,575
- Let's go.
- Oh, my.

511
00:30:11,575 --> 00:30:13,443
Hello.

512
00:30:13,443 --> 00:30:15,426
Oh, hey there.

513
00:30:16,879 --> 00:30:19,235
- Can we get off?
- Oh, sure.

514
00:30:19,235 --> 00:30:21,126
- Yes, sorry.
- Let's go, Yul.

515
00:30:24,379 --> 00:30:26,079
Oh, yeah.

516
00:30:27,487 --> 00:30:30,011
- Let's go.
- Whoa.

517
00:30:30,611 --> 00:30:33,187
Why did I just get a chill down my spine?

518
00:30:33,187 --> 00:30:35,487
What, is something wrong?

519
00:30:35,487 --> 00:30:37,095
- Huh?
- Grandma!

520
00:30:37,095 --> 00:30:39,626
Oh, my baby is here?

521
00:30:39,626 --> 00:30:42,231
Mother, did someone come by?

522
00:30:42,231 --> 00:30:43,767
Yeah, a bank employee.

523
00:30:43,767 --> 00:30:45,595
Oh, the young man worked so hard.

524
00:30:45,595 --> 00:30:48,035
He couldn't even leave work
and came all the way to a customer's house.

525
00:30:48,035 --> 00:30:49,223
A bank employee?

526
00:30:49,223 --> 00:30:51,167
Yeah.

527
00:30:51,167 --> 00:30:53,159
Mother, did you give him the money?

528
00:30:53,159 --> 00:30:54,331
Of course, I did.

529
00:30:54,331 --> 00:30:56,231
He came to collect the loan repayment.

530
00:30:56,231 --> 00:30:58,326
The savings payout I got today...

531
00:30:59,747 --> 00:31:01,999
Why? What's wrong?

532
00:31:01,999 --> 00:31:04,239
Mother, this really
looks like voice phishing.

533
00:31:04,239 --> 00:31:06,259
- Stay home with Yul. Okay?
- What?

534
00:31:06,892 --> 00:31:08,592
What?

535
00:31:09,819 --> 00:31:11,519
Oh, my God!

536
00:31:12,819 --> 00:31:15,326
What do I do?

537
00:31:28,407 --> 00:31:29,877
Oh, seriously.

538
00:31:32,544 --> 00:31:33,663
Oh, she's...

539
00:31:33,663 --> 00:31:35,583
What is she going to do?

540
00:31:35,583 --> 00:31:37,279
What?

541
00:31:37,279 --> 00:31:39,244
Huh? That woman from earlier.

542
00:31:39,244 --> 00:31:40,944
Darn it.

543
00:31:41,727 --> 00:31:42,915
You, get out.

544
00:31:42,915 --> 00:31:46,088
What? Did she figure me out?

545
00:31:46,088 --> 00:31:47,826
Darn it!

546
00:31:56,890 --> 00:31:58,267
Oh! Darn it!

547
00:31:58,267 --> 00:32:00,723
Has that punk lost her mind?

548
00:32:00,723 --> 00:32:02,559
You want to play, huh?

549
00:32:13,871 --> 00:32:15,571
Oh, that startled me!

550
00:32:16,959 --> 00:32:19,292
Oh, my!

551
00:32:23,726 --> 00:32:24,726
Oh, my heart.

552
00:32:24,726 --> 00:32:27,274
Wait, what did I just see?

553
00:32:27,274 --> 00:32:30,559
- <i>Yes, Ms. Yoo.</i>
- Can you run a license plate for me?

554
00:32:30,559 --> 00:32:31,843
- Se Ah!
- Bo Na!

555
00:32:31,843 --> 00:32:32,911
Where are you going?

556
00:32:32,911 --> 00:32:34,939
I need to catch that car.
It's voice phishing.

557
00:32:34,939 --> 00:32:37,151
What? Voice phishing?

558
00:32:37,151 --> 00:32:38,383
T-T-That one over there?

559
00:32:38,383 --> 00:32:39,892
Yeah.

560
00:32:39,892 --> 00:32:41,059
Assistant Manager Ki, I've got this.

561
00:32:41,059 --> 00:32:42,759
Wait, Ms. Yoo...

562
00:32:49,128 --> 00:32:50,828
Voice phishing?

563
00:32:52,823 --> 00:32:54,992
Then those two women...

564
00:32:56,785 --> 00:32:58,485
Wow.

565
00:32:59,579 --> 00:33:02,092
Of all the people to mess with...

566
00:33:03,626 --> 00:33:06,939
But Bo Na, why are you chasing him?

567
00:33:06,939 --> 00:33:08,747
Who's the victim?

568
00:33:08,747 --> 00:33:11,459
Mother. He ran off with her savings.

569
00:33:11,459 --> 00:33:13,651
What? That crazy punk!

570
00:33:13,651 --> 00:33:15,492
Hold on tight, Bo Na!

571
00:33:31,999 --> 00:33:33,331
Se Ah, drop me off over there.

572
00:33:33,331 --> 00:33:34,951
What? Why?

573
00:33:34,951 --> 00:33:36,895
Hurry.

574
00:33:36,895 --> 00:33:39,426
What are you planning to do?

575
00:33:40,995 --> 00:33:42,392
I have to get Mother's money back.

576
00:33:42,392 --> 00:33:43,859
I'll see you at home. I'm going.

577
00:33:43,859 --> 00:33:45,306
You're going alone?

578
00:33:45,306 --> 00:33:47,859
Bo Na, please be careful.

579
00:33:48,647 --> 00:33:50,526
I'm going to get you.

580
00:34:18,621 --> 00:34:20,363
Darn it.

581
00:34:20,363 --> 00:34:22,826
Man, I've been running a lot lately.

582
00:34:35,687 --> 00:34:37,392
Why are you following me?

583
00:34:54,892 --> 00:34:56,859
- Are you okay?
- Are you all right?

584
00:35:29,492 --> 00:35:31,740
What?

585
00:35:31,740 --> 00:35:34,140
Oh, my! Darn it!

586
00:35:45,893 --> 00:35:48,291
What? Are you police?

587
00:35:48,291 --> 00:35:49,863
Someone scarier than the police.

588
00:35:49,863 --> 00:35:51,771
Darn it!

589
00:35:51,771 --> 00:35:56,592
You're not even a cop, lady,
but you've seriously got no fear.

590
00:35:57,379 --> 00:35:58,571
What are you going to do?

591
00:35:58,571 --> 00:36:01,923
There's no one around,
and there aren't any CCTV cameras either.

592
00:36:01,923 --> 00:36:03,915
Is that so?

593
00:36:03,915 --> 00:36:05,699
Perfect. Get up.

594
00:36:05,699 --> 00:36:07,399
What?

595
00:36:08,259 --> 00:36:10,926
[Seoul Nambu Police Station]

596
00:36:14,287 --> 00:36:16,139
Can we get Mother's money back right away?

597
00:36:16,139 --> 00:36:17,199
I'm worried she might collapse.

598
00:36:17,199 --> 00:36:18,199
Ms. Bo Na!

599
00:36:18,199 --> 00:36:20,559
- Kwon Se Ah!
- Mr. Dong Jin.

600
00:36:20,559 --> 00:36:21,611
Oh, hello.

601
00:36:21,611 --> 00:36:23,659
Ms. Bo Na, are you alright?

602
00:36:23,659 --> 00:36:24,692
Yes, I'm fine.

603
00:36:24,692 --> 00:36:26,867
You were busy.
What brought you all the way here?

604
00:36:26,867 --> 00:36:29,463
Why did you chase them? It was dangerous.
You weren't hurt, were you?

605
00:36:29,463 --> 00:36:30,826
I'm fine.

606
00:36:30,826 --> 00:36:32,655
Thank you for worrying about me.

607
00:36:32,655 --> 00:36:33,795
- Oh, Mr. Lee.
- Sorry.

608
00:36:33,795 --> 00:36:35,047
Do you know her?

609
00:36:35,047 --> 00:36:37,115
Yeah, she's family.

610
00:36:37,115 --> 00:36:39,599
What? Family?

611
00:36:39,599 --> 00:36:40,999
Oh, what about the voice-phishing scammers?

612
00:36:40,999 --> 00:36:43,026
Oh, they're over there.

613
00:36:44,524 --> 00:36:45,643
What's wrong with those punks?

614
00:36:45,643 --> 00:36:47,175
Looks like they fell and rolled around

615
00:36:47,175 --> 00:36:50,307
while trying to get away from these ladies.

616
00:36:50,307 --> 00:36:52,299
No, that's not what happened!

617
00:36:52,299 --> 00:36:55,759
That wretch in red threw me
with a hip toss! Three times, even!

618
00:36:55,759 --> 00:36:58,831
And that lady hit me with a Coke,

619
00:36:58,831 --> 00:37:01,399
kicked me here, and kneed me here. Look!

620
00:37:01,399 --> 00:37:02,495
A knee kick?

621
00:37:02,495 --> 00:37:05,526
Seriously, they were fighting
among themselves and ended up falling over.

622
00:37:05,526 --> 00:37:07,226
Wow, that's pretty funny, huh?

623
00:37:07,226 --> 00:37:10,899
When can we get Mother's money back...

624
00:37:10,899 --> 00:37:13,592
Well, it takes a little longer because
we have to go through that procedure.

625
00:37:13,592 --> 00:37:14,695
- Really?
- Even after being caught...

626
00:37:14,695 --> 00:37:17,751
These guys still haven't come to
their senses. They're still talking nonsense.

627
00:37:17,751 --> 00:37:19,526
Looks like it. Hey, you punk. Come here!

628
00:37:19,526 --> 00:37:22,159
What, "that wretch"?
Who are you calling a wretch?

629
00:37:22,159 --> 00:37:23,859
Hey, get that mouth over here.

630
00:37:23,859 --> 00:37:26,819
- I'll kill you if I get in there.
- So cool.

631
00:37:26,819 --> 00:37:28,392
Honey!

632
00:37:28,392 --> 00:37:29,719
- Goodness, dear!
- Mother.

633
00:37:29,719 --> 00:37:31,055
Mom, Tae Seong!

634
00:37:31,055 --> 00:37:32,923
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

635
00:37:32,923 --> 00:37:35,563
I'm perfectly fine, honey. Don't worry.

636
00:37:35,563 --> 00:37:37,192
Are you really okay?

637
00:37:37,192 --> 00:37:38,771
I'm perfectly fine, really.

638
00:37:38,771 --> 00:37:40,467
Oh, jeez.

639
00:37:40,467 --> 00:37:43,695
My money! Sir, what about my money?

640
00:37:43,695 --> 00:37:47,559
We'll return it to you after the procedures,
so don't worry too much.

641
00:37:47,559 --> 00:37:49,927
Oh, thank goodness.

642
00:37:49,927 --> 00:37:52,892
That money means everything to me.

643
00:37:52,892 --> 00:37:55,559
It's usually hard to get your money back
once you've been scammed.

644
00:37:55,559 --> 00:37:58,492
These two ladies really
did something incredible.

645
00:37:58,492 --> 00:38:00,326
- Why...
- Why did you even chase after him?

646
00:38:00,326 --> 00:38:02,579
You should've called the police.

647
00:38:02,579 --> 00:38:04,144
Do you have any idea how scared I was?

648
00:38:04,144 --> 00:38:06,392
- I just happened to see it.
- Excuse me, Tae Seong.

649
00:38:06,392 --> 00:38:09,155
Can't you see your one
and only little sister here?

650
00:38:09,155 --> 00:38:10,763
Of course, you're fine.

651
00:38:10,763 --> 00:38:12,224
- Why are you saying that?
- Why would you do something

652
00:38:12,224 --> 00:38:14,811
- so dangerous...
- Show a little more heartfelt concern!

653
00:38:14,811 --> 00:38:16,755
I have absolute faith in your well-being.

654
00:38:16,755 --> 00:38:18,792
- Oh, seriously...
- Stop having so much faith in me!

655
00:38:19,427 --> 00:38:20,607
Why?

656
00:38:21,471 --> 00:38:23,811
Why does getting my own money back
have to involve

657
00:38:23,811 --> 00:38:25,779
- such complicated procedures?
- Tell me about it.

658
00:38:25,779 --> 00:38:28,226
Man, I'm back here again.

659
00:38:28,226 --> 00:38:29,997
Another criminal caught.

660
00:38:29,997 --> 00:38:32,559
- What a fulfilling day.
- Oh, dear.

661
00:38:33,755 --> 00:38:39,126
But even so, that's too much.
You didn't have to go that far.

662
00:38:40,035 --> 00:38:41,375
No.

663
00:38:41,375 --> 00:38:45,951
It's your hard-earned money, saved up
penny by penny from dawn to dusk.

664
00:38:45,951 --> 00:38:47,651
Of course, we had to get it back.

665
00:38:48,847 --> 00:38:53,792
Anyway, I'd have been
in serious trouble without you.

666
00:38:53,792 --> 00:38:55,526
Than...

667
00:38:56,215 --> 00:38:57,915
Than...

668
00:38:58,707 --> 00:39:00,407
Than...

669
00:39:01,535 --> 00:39:04,203
Then let's go get some meat.

670
00:39:04,203 --> 00:39:07,459
Is it really that hard to say thank you?

671
00:39:09,039 --> 00:39:10,611
Let's go, Se Ah.

672
00:39:10,611 --> 00:39:12,092
Mother, let's go together!

673
00:39:12,092 --> 00:39:14,915
Is that pride or just stubbornness?

674
00:39:14,915 --> 00:39:16,615
Kwon Se Ah!

675
00:39:22,995 --> 00:39:25,126
Are you seriously leaving
without saying goodbye?

676
00:39:32,599 --> 00:39:33,839
Why are you avoiding me?

677
00:39:33,839 --> 00:39:37,503
When did I? I'm not avoiding you.

678
00:39:37,503 --> 00:39:38,695
Did I do something wrong?

679
00:39:38,695 --> 00:39:40,371
No.

680
00:39:40,371 --> 00:39:44,526
It's not that you did anything wrong...

681
00:39:44,526 --> 00:39:46,691
Why are you trailing off like that?
That's not like you.

682
00:39:46,691 --> 00:39:49,023
Hey, just spit it out. What is it?

683
00:39:49,023 --> 00:39:51,492
Do you...

684
00:39:54,587 --> 00:39:56,675
Stop beating around the bush and just say it.

685
00:39:56,675 --> 00:39:57,935
What about me?

686
00:39:57,935 --> 00:39:59,792
Do you like me?

687
00:40:07,959 --> 00:40:11,592
Hey, that's why you...
You're seriously funny.

688
00:40:12,463 --> 00:40:14,995
Hey, what's so funny about that?

689
00:40:14,995 --> 00:40:16,407
Forget it if not!

690
00:40:16,407 --> 00:40:20,363
I was just asking
because I wondered. That's all.

691
00:40:20,363 --> 00:40:23,292
Seriously, you drive me crazy.

692
00:40:26,659 --> 00:40:28,479
Oh, that's what it is!

693
00:40:28,479 --> 00:40:31,091
What? What is it?

694
00:40:31,091 --> 00:40:32,893
So that's why I've been like this lately,

695
00:40:32,893 --> 00:40:36,703
getting annoyed when I can't reach you,
wondering what you're doing,

696
00:40:36,703 --> 00:40:39,726
wanting to see your face
and hear your voice. Now I get it...

697
00:40:40,799 --> 00:40:42,892
What?

698
00:40:42,892 --> 00:40:45,192
Huh, you're right.

699
00:40:48,135 --> 00:40:49,959
I guess I do like you.

700
00:41:02,663 --> 00:41:06,192
I'll let you know when the results come out.
It'll take a few days.

701
00:41:08,063 --> 00:41:09,807
Thanks for coming, even though you're busy.

702
00:41:09,807 --> 00:41:11,431
Don't even mention it.

703
00:41:11,431 --> 00:41:14,126
It's your wife's matter. How could I not go?

704
00:41:16,227 --> 00:41:17,803
I guess married couples
really do start to look alike.

705
00:41:17,803 --> 00:41:21,592
How did she have the guts
to chase them like that?

706
00:41:21,592 --> 00:41:24,959
She doesn't take after me.
She's always been fearless.

707
00:41:24,959 --> 00:41:27,479
I suppose she's different from you,
always getting stabbed in the back.

708
00:41:27,479 --> 00:41:28,611
Jeez, give me a break.

709
00:41:28,611 --> 00:41:32,459
Hey, Bo Na was the one
who hit him with a Coke bottle.

710
00:41:33,423 --> 00:41:34,526
What?

711
00:41:34,526 --> 00:41:39,092
Maybe Bo Na should be protecting you
instead of the other way around.

712
00:41:40,615 --> 00:41:42,875
Come on, I'm not that bad.

713
00:41:42,875 --> 00:41:44,575
Jeez.

714
00:41:47,015 --> 00:41:49,767
Actually, I wanted to ask you something.
Good timing.

715
00:41:49,767 --> 00:41:51,859
- Ask me something?
- Yeah.

716
00:41:54,703 --> 00:41:57,779
That man you said you saw.

717
00:41:57,779 --> 00:41:59,479
Kingfisher.

718
00:42:00,831 --> 00:42:02,359
Hey, don't talk about that until I say...

719
00:42:02,359 --> 00:42:04,059
Hear me out first.

720
00:42:05,682 --> 00:42:08,659
Isn't it possible you saw him wrong?

721
00:42:10,327 --> 00:42:13,503
Why do you assume I was wrong
before even hearing me out?

722
00:42:13,503 --> 00:42:15,651
I ask you a question,
and you answer with another question?

723
00:42:15,651 --> 00:42:16,979
Then next question.

724
00:42:16,979 --> 00:42:19,971
Eight years ago, during the World Cup
pickpocketing case,

725
00:42:19,971 --> 00:42:23,247
did you ever find the woman
who called an ambulance for you?

726
00:42:23,247 --> 00:42:26,107
How am I supposed to find someone
I couldn't find back then?

727
00:42:26,107 --> 00:42:29,792
If I'd found her, I'd have met her
long ago. She saved my life.

728
00:42:30,515 --> 00:42:31,843
But why are you suddenly asking about her?

729
00:42:31,843 --> 00:42:33,939
There should be a recording
of her voice on your phone.

730
00:42:33,939 --> 00:42:35,959
Reporters usually have automatic
call recording turned on.

731
00:42:35,959 --> 00:42:37,159
Didn't you listen to it?

732
00:42:37,159 --> 00:42:40,383
Of course, I did. Right after I woke up.

733
00:42:40,383 --> 00:42:41,759
But how would listening to
her voice tell me who she is?

734
00:42:41,759 --> 00:42:45,935
Am I supposed to compare her voice
with every woman's in Korea?

735
00:42:45,935 --> 00:42:49,307
Do you still have that phone?

736
00:42:49,307 --> 00:42:50,883
The one from back then?

737
00:42:50,883 --> 00:42:53,103
Yeah.

738
00:42:53,103 --> 00:42:56,199
I got rid of it ages ago. That was years ago.

739
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:58,826
Why are you looking for her anyway?

740
00:43:03,426 --> 00:43:09,292
She could have witnessed Kingfisher
or been an accomplice.

741
00:43:09,983 --> 00:43:11,683
Or...

742
00:43:12,315 --> 00:43:14,426
she could even be Kingfisher herself.

743
00:43:15,391 --> 00:43:17,091
What?

744
00:43:17,815 --> 00:43:19,892
Tae Seong,

745
00:43:19,892 --> 00:43:23,091
stop withholding information
and confusing me.

746
00:43:23,091 --> 00:43:26,079
Otherwise, I'll send you
an official summons soon.

747
00:43:26,079 --> 00:43:29,192
You know I'm on the Kingfisher
task force now, right?

748
00:43:39,455 --> 00:43:41,199
Wow!

749
00:43:41,199 --> 00:43:44,711
The meat is really good today.
Where did you get it?

750
00:43:44,711 --> 00:43:47,213
It's Sangju beef. Sangju beef.

751
00:43:47,213 --> 00:43:53,026
I asked for the very best cut,
so eat as much as you want today.

752
00:43:53,026 --> 00:43:54,826
- Thank you.
- Okay!

753
00:43:56,295 --> 00:44:00,692
She was begging for beef all day.
Why isn't she eating?

754
00:44:00,692 --> 00:44:04,026
Leave her alone.
Maybe she's full without eating.

755
00:44:05,809 --> 00:44:07,303
What's wrong with him now?

756
00:44:07,303 --> 00:44:09,315
Hey, the meat's going to burn.

757
00:44:09,315 --> 00:44:11,026
Yeah.

758
00:44:12,323 --> 00:44:14,926
Oh, flowers.

759
00:44:14,926 --> 00:44:16,575
Yul's mom bought them.

760
00:44:16,575 --> 00:44:19,992
That really brightens up the whole place.

761
00:44:21,595 --> 00:44:26,035
I got them at the flower shop up front
while I was coming here, Mother.

762
00:44:26,035 --> 00:44:29,992
I heard sunflowers cleanse
a home of negative energy

763
00:44:29,992 --> 00:44:33,192
and fill it with bright, positive energy.

764
00:44:34,383 --> 00:44:36,059
So that's what sunflowers mean.

765
00:44:36,059 --> 00:44:39,327
Seriously though, you're something else.

766
00:44:39,327 --> 00:44:43,359
How did you even think to chase
them down with your bare hands?

767
00:44:43,359 --> 00:44:45,559
Oh, well, that's...

768
00:44:46,451 --> 00:44:49,810
I think my body just reacted first.

769
00:44:49,810 --> 00:44:51,167
Right away!

770
00:44:51,167 --> 00:44:52,443
Especially with Se Ah there, I was just...

771
00:44:52,443 --> 00:44:54,143
That's impressive.

772
00:44:56,251 --> 00:44:58,087
Mother, the beef is so good.

773
00:44:58,087 --> 00:45:00,191
Yes, it's good.

774
00:45:00,191 --> 00:45:01,407
Eat up.

775
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:05,526
Yul, have another bite.
It's not too hot, is it?

776
00:45:05,526 --> 00:45:07,203
Don't ever do that again.

777
00:45:07,203 --> 00:45:09,759
Make sure you call the police first, okay?

778
00:45:09,759 --> 00:45:13,683
Whether your mom gets scammed or not,
you only care about your wife.

779
00:45:13,683 --> 00:45:15,283
Here you go again.

780
00:45:15,283 --> 00:45:17,443
Mom, are you proud of getting scammed?

781
00:45:17,443 --> 00:45:19,026
Wow. How could you fall for that?

782
00:45:19,026 --> 00:45:20,979
You're really rubbing salt in the wound.

783
00:45:20,979 --> 00:45:23,015
Let's see if you'd have fallen for it
if you got that call.

784
00:45:23,015 --> 00:45:24,392
I wouldn't.

785
00:45:24,392 --> 00:45:25,692
It's good.

786
00:45:25,692 --> 00:45:27,895
They couldn't find any other way
to get money? Huh?

787
00:45:27,895 --> 00:45:30,978
Steal someone's
hard-earned money like that? Huh?

788
00:45:30,978 --> 00:45:32,047
Wow, that's good enough.

789
00:45:32,047 --> 00:45:33,892
Try some rice too.

790
00:45:39,192 --> 00:45:41,559
This is really good.

791
00:45:42,379 --> 00:45:45,015
This is all cooked.

792
00:45:45,015 --> 00:45:50,826
Do you know how much effort I put in today?

793
00:46:05,735 --> 00:46:07,451
Honey! I'll do it.

794
00:46:07,451 --> 00:46:08,726
No, it's fine. Why are you doing this?

795
00:46:08,726 --> 00:46:09,726
- I'll do it.
- It'll only take a minute.

796
00:46:09,726 --> 00:46:10,731
- No, don't.
- Honey...

797
00:46:10,731 --> 00:46:12,459
Kwon Tae Seong!

798
00:46:17,511 --> 00:46:18,592
Mom, that's not it...

799
00:46:18,592 --> 00:46:22,459
The women did all the cooking,
so I'll at least do the dishes.

800
00:46:26,467 --> 00:46:29,519
There's a lot of grease, so use hot water.

801
00:46:29,519 --> 00:46:32,159
And rinse everything really well, okay?

802
00:46:40,955 --> 00:46:42,655
Here.

803
00:46:47,795 --> 00:46:50,326
Pull your clothes up a little.

804
00:46:51,223 --> 00:46:52,923
Okay.

805
00:47:03,355 --> 00:47:05,526
- Pears cost more now.
- Mom, didn't you get any pears?

806
00:47:05,526 --> 00:47:07,619
I made time and got everything.

807
00:47:07,619 --> 00:47:11,292
Come on, Mom, I told you not to.

808
00:47:11,292 --> 00:47:14,326
- What?
- Hey!

809
00:47:14,326 --> 00:47:16,959
[Ok's Flower Shop]

810
00:47:32,826 --> 00:47:37,726
[Interviews with Kingfisher's
Victims' Associates]

811
00:47:48,771 --> 00:47:50,711
<i>Why are you looking for her anyway?</i>

812
00:47:50,711 --> 00:47:55,459
She could have witnessed Kingfisher
or been an accomplice.

813
00:47:56,267 --> 00:47:59,726
<i>Or she could even be Kingfisher herself.</i>

814
00:48:20,219 --> 00:48:23,023
<i>Your husband stopped by the shop today.</i>

815
00:48:23,023 --> 00:48:25,247
<i>It seems he went looking for Cheol.</i>

816
00:48:25,247 --> 00:48:27,926
[Team Leader Bae]
<i>He asked about the flower sender.</i>

817
00:48:29,175 --> 00:48:33,492
<i>I gave him a vague answer,
but I thought you should know.</i>

818
00:48:44,526 --> 00:48:46,326
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

819
00:48:46,326 --> 00:48:49,192
The shooter was definitely just one person.

820
00:48:49,192 --> 00:48:50,667
But as you can see,

821
00:48:50,667 --> 00:48:53,087
there may have been an accomplice
involved in everything besides the shooting.

822
00:48:53,087 --> 00:48:57,859
We can't rule out the possibility of
a separate team operating independently.

823
00:48:57,859 --> 00:49:01,926
Kingfisher may have an organized
group of accomplices?

824
00:49:03,331 --> 00:49:04,603
That's plausible.

825
00:49:04,603 --> 00:49:05,667
Yes.

826
00:49:05,667 --> 00:49:07,959
If that's the case,
it's highly likely their methods

827
00:49:07,959 --> 00:49:10,519
go beyond simply carrying out sniper attacks,

828
00:49:10,519 --> 00:49:13,391
based on what we've uncovered so far.

829
00:49:13,391 --> 00:49:14,731
What is that supposed to mean?

830
00:49:14,731 --> 00:49:17,259
[Kingfisher Special Task Force]
If it's not a shooting, then what?

831
00:49:19,583 --> 00:49:20,827
[Analysis of Staged Accidental Deaths]
Pyo Kyu Cheol?

832
00:49:20,827 --> 00:49:22,515
Hey, he was shot and killed.

833
00:49:22,515 --> 00:49:25,447
I believe Kingfisher's side originally
planned to make it look like an accident,

834
00:49:25,447 --> 00:49:29,739
but some variable arose, forcing him
to finish the job with a shooting.

835
00:49:29,739 --> 00:49:31,439
What's the basis for that?

836
00:49:32,995 --> 00:49:36,319
We tracked eight serious child sex offenders

837
00:49:36,319 --> 00:49:39,591
from the past 15 years
since Kingfisher first appeared.

838
00:49:39,591 --> 00:49:44,071
All eight were confirmed
to have died in various accidents,

839
00:49:44,071 --> 00:49:47,287
car crashes, falls, electrocution,
drowning, and so on.

840
00:49:47,287 --> 00:49:50,247
While Kingfisher draws
attention with a shooting,

841
00:49:50,247 --> 00:49:54,826
a separate team eliminates criminals
by disguising their deaths as accidents?

842
00:49:56,383 --> 00:49:58,931
That's an interesting theory.

843
00:49:58,931 --> 00:50:00,607
Hey.

844
00:50:00,607 --> 00:50:02,592
Ms. Yoo, why are you doing this too?

845
00:50:03,511 --> 00:50:06,609
We tracked 20 serious criminals
who received relatively light sentences

846
00:50:06,609 --> 00:50:09,423
and were released over the past 15 years.

847
00:50:09,423 --> 00:50:12,359
11 were killed by Kingfisher's shootings,

848
00:50:12,359 --> 00:50:15,247
while 8 died in apparent accidents.

849
00:50:15,247 --> 00:50:17,303
And...

850
00:50:17,303 --> 00:50:19,559
the most recent victim, Hwang Cheol Beom.

851
00:50:19,559 --> 00:50:20,592
[Hwang Cheol Beom]

852
00:50:20,592 --> 00:50:23,627
He was so afraid of Kingfisher
that he voluntarily went back to prison,

853
00:50:23,627 --> 00:50:26,571
but he was found dead
inside the prison last week.

854
00:50:26,571 --> 00:50:29,292
The cause of death was cardiac arrest.

855
00:50:29,292 --> 00:50:30,867
Good grief.

856
00:50:30,867 --> 00:50:34,749
Some died in accidents. Others from illness.

857
00:50:34,749 --> 00:50:36,747
Are we a criminal obituary
task force or what?

858
00:50:36,747 --> 00:50:41,292
If 19 out of 20 are dead,

859
00:50:42,063 --> 00:50:43,763
who's the one that hasn't died yet?

860
00:50:47,715 --> 00:50:49,063
<i>Gu Jong Ryeol.</i>

861
00:50:49,063 --> 00:50:50,792
About two years ago,

862
00:50:50,792 --> 00:50:56,092
<i>a four-year-old child died shortly
after being brought to the emergency room.</i>

863
00:50:56,092 --> 00:50:57,592
<i>You remember that case, right?</i>

864
00:50:57,592 --> 00:50:59,379
<i>According to the medical records at the time,</i>

865
00:50:59,379 --> 00:51:02,387
the abdomen was filled with blood
due to internal organ bleeding,

866
00:51:02,387 --> 00:51:04,237
and there were fractures all over the body,

867
00:51:04,237 --> 00:51:06,683
but the fractures
occurred at different times.

868
00:51:06,683 --> 00:51:09,683
My gosh. What did they do to that child?

869
00:51:09,683 --> 00:51:14,079
A police investigation
revealed horrific child abuse.

870
00:51:14,079 --> 00:51:15,919
The adoptive mom, as the main culprit,
was sentenced to 9 years,

871
00:51:15,919 --> 00:51:19,227
and the biological dad,
Gu Jong Ryeol, got 2 years for neglect.

872
00:51:19,227 --> 00:51:21,063
Their sentences are ridiculous.

873
00:51:21,063 --> 00:51:22,759
The abuse was acknowledged,

874
00:51:22,759 --> 00:51:25,887
but the court found no implied intent
regarding the child's death,

875
00:51:25,887 --> 00:51:29,239
so they were charged with
injury causing death, not murder.

876
00:51:29,239 --> 00:51:33,423
The six-year-old sister also gave
testimony favorable to the parents.

877
00:51:33,423 --> 00:51:35,359
Is there a chance Gu Jong Ryeol
genuinely didn't know?

878
00:51:35,359 --> 00:51:37,792
[Client Information]
The daughter later recanted her testimony.

879
00:51:37,792 --> 00:51:41,183
She said her dad
had abused the child as well.

880
00:51:41,183 --> 00:51:45,692
But it wasn't accepted because her statements
were considered inconsistent.

881
00:51:45,692 --> 00:51:47,895
Where's the daughter now?

882
00:51:47,895 --> 00:51:51,426
She's not living with her dad, is she?

883
00:51:52,287 --> 00:51:55,451
She was taken away right after it happened
and is now in a child care center.

884
00:51:55,451 --> 00:51:58,126
Well, that's a relief.

885
00:51:58,743 --> 00:52:00,759
So what about Gu Jong Ryeol?

886
00:52:01,635 --> 00:52:06,187
I believe he's highly likely to be
Kingfisher's next target.

887
00:52:06,187 --> 00:52:07,431
Who wants to take this one?

888
00:52:07,431 --> 00:52:09,192
- Me.
- I will.

889
00:52:14,153 --> 00:52:15,331
What's going on?

890
00:52:15,331 --> 00:52:19,535
Since when did you become
such in-sync partners?

891
00:52:19,535 --> 00:52:21,431
No way!

892
00:52:21,431 --> 00:52:24,299
Right? There's no way you two are, huh?

893
00:52:24,299 --> 00:52:25,495
No!

894
00:52:25,495 --> 00:52:29,563
Anyway, we need to keep
a low profile for the time being,

895
00:52:29,563 --> 00:52:30,999
so you two handle this case.

896
00:52:30,999 --> 00:52:33,431
And Assistant Manager Ki,
make sure there's solid support.

897
00:52:33,431 --> 00:52:35,695
Understood.

898
00:52:35,695 --> 00:52:37,811
<i>What? Use Gu Jong Ryeol?</i>

899
00:52:37,811 --> 00:52:41,795
We'll set a trap around Gu Jong Ryeol
before Kingfisher makes a move.

900
00:52:41,795 --> 00:52:46,711
Are you suggesting we work
with a criminal to set up a sting?

901
00:52:46,711 --> 00:52:48,603
I'm suggesting we use it as an opportunity.

902
00:52:48,603 --> 00:52:51,392
Isn't the evidence too weak
to say for certain that

903
00:52:51,392 --> 00:52:53,367
Gu Jong Ryeol is the next target?

904
00:52:53,367 --> 00:52:56,626
For now, I think it's our only lead
to catching Kingfisher.

905
00:52:56,626 --> 00:52:57,991
Wait.

906
00:52:57,991 --> 00:53:02,339
If we go by what you say,
there's no guarantee he'll use a gun,

907
00:53:02,339 --> 00:53:06,607
so how can we jump into this without knowing
when, where, or how he'll strike?

908
00:53:06,607 --> 00:53:09,951
Deploying equipment and personnel
based on speculation alone

909
00:53:09,951 --> 00:53:12,867
is like banging our heads against a wall.

910
00:53:12,867 --> 00:53:15,531
Mr. Gu, I think this has
a real chance of working.

911
00:53:15,531 --> 00:53:16,835
Please hear me out a little longer...

912
00:53:16,835 --> 00:53:19,475
What more is there to hear?

913
00:53:19,475 --> 00:53:21,175
Mr. Gu!

914
00:53:22,651 --> 00:53:24,351
Go for it.

915
00:53:25,303 --> 00:53:27,003
What?

916
00:53:27,783 --> 00:53:30,331
But you can't make direct
contact with Gu Jong Ryeol.

917
00:53:30,331 --> 00:53:34,303
Teaming up with a criminal to catch
a criminal? Does that make sense?

918
00:53:34,303 --> 00:53:37,379
Second, I can't convince the higher-ups
without solid evidence.

919
00:53:37,379 --> 00:53:40,455
So I can't provide equipment
or personnel support right now.

920
00:53:40,455 --> 00:53:44,019
Third, I can't give you unlimited time.

921
00:53:44,019 --> 00:53:45,683
For now, Mr. Lee, work on
this one on your own.

922
00:53:45,683 --> 00:53:48,283
You two can stake out for 24 hours
or keep surveillance.

923
00:53:48,283 --> 00:53:49,491
You have exactly one week.

924
00:53:49,491 --> 00:53:51,495
If you manage to get any lead
on Kingfisher within that time,

925
00:53:51,495 --> 00:53:53,192
I'll stake my team leader position

926
00:53:53,192 --> 00:53:56,827
and give you all the support you want. Okay?

927
00:53:56,827 --> 00:53:58,527
Alright, meeting's over!

928
00:53:59,726 --> 00:54:00,826
Oh, boy.

929
00:54:00,826 --> 00:54:03,159
- It'll be a waste of effort.
- Oh, dear.

930
00:54:04,384 --> 00:54:06,084
Oh, jeez.

931
00:54:07,126 --> 00:54:09,191
[Used PC Sales and Repair]

932
00:54:09,191 --> 00:54:10,992
Here you go.

933
00:54:14,975 --> 00:54:18,271
The voice recordings
and other data are all still intact, right?

934
00:54:18,271 --> 00:54:22,259
Of course. I only replaced the battery,
so all the data inside is still intact.

935
00:54:33,495 --> 00:54:35,859
Assistant Manager Ki went down first.

936
00:55:03,426 --> 00:55:05,215
You always seem to have venom in your veins.

937
00:55:05,215 --> 00:55:06,603
Of course.

938
00:55:06,603 --> 00:55:08,987
You're very wary.

939
00:55:08,987 --> 00:55:10,615
Did you have a rough childhood?

940
00:55:10,615 --> 00:55:12,395
I had a childhood as miserable as anyone's.

941
00:55:12,395 --> 00:55:14,351
I don't even know what my parents look like.

942
00:55:14,351 --> 00:55:17,203
Must've been nice, not having a dad.

943
00:55:17,203 --> 00:55:19,992
You must at least know when you were born.

944
00:55:19,992 --> 00:55:21,559
I know exactly.

945
00:55:21,559 --> 00:55:24,492
Because I broke a rib on my fifth birthday.

946
00:55:34,239 --> 00:55:37,047
You can break a rib even without a dad.

947
00:55:37,047 --> 00:55:38,759
An arm or a leg too.

948
00:56:02,507 --> 00:56:04,111
I'll back you up too.

949
00:56:04,111 --> 00:56:05,926
Director Yoo!

950
00:56:07,092 --> 00:56:09,826
You're really going to back me up?

951
00:56:13,663 --> 00:56:16,126
Let's see what you two can do.

952
00:56:18,375 --> 00:56:20,399
You're driving too?

953
00:56:20,399 --> 00:56:22,426
Hurry up, let's go.

954
00:56:22,426 --> 00:56:24,126
Come on out!

955
00:56:29,603 --> 00:56:31,759
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

956
00:56:40,947 --> 00:56:42,751
Keep a close watch.

957
00:56:42,751 --> 00:56:44,279
On what?

958
00:56:44,279 --> 00:56:45,895
I mean, Yoo Bo Na.

959
00:56:45,895 --> 00:56:48,359
If something feels off, we'll call off
the meeting immediately.

960
00:56:48,359 --> 00:56:50,059
Ms. Bo Na?

961
00:56:51,619 --> 00:56:54,995
Is something bugging you?

962
00:56:54,995 --> 00:56:58,992
This client makes me think of someone.

963
00:57:00,592 --> 00:57:03,499
Some memories from childhood

964
00:57:03,499 --> 00:57:06,126
don't fade easily, you know.

965
00:57:14,395 --> 00:57:17,123
If he approves it,
he needs to give us their full support.

966
00:57:17,123 --> 00:57:20,359
This isn't really approval,
but it's not a refusal either.

967
00:57:21,263 --> 00:57:24,959
At least assign a few people
to relieve us on the stakeout.

968
00:57:30,315 --> 00:57:33,107
Looks like you have a lot on your mind.

969
00:57:33,107 --> 00:57:38,175
Do you think Kingfisher could be a woman?

970
00:57:38,175 --> 00:57:39,875
Huh?

971
00:57:40,583 --> 00:57:42,683
Well...

972
00:57:42,683 --> 00:57:45,426
I think it's quite possible.

973
00:57:47,935 --> 00:57:49,623
A foreigner?

974
00:57:49,623 --> 00:57:51,959
That seems possible too.

975
00:57:51,959 --> 00:57:53,471
What about a minor?

976
00:57:53,471 --> 00:57:55,326
There's no reason to rule it out.

977
00:57:57,767 --> 00:57:59,467
Right.

978
00:58:00,443 --> 00:58:03,773
Based on my gut,
there's definitely a secret organization

979
00:58:03,773 --> 00:58:05,495
like a "Dark Death Squad" behind Kingfisher.

980
00:58:05,495 --> 00:58:08,247
They disguise themselves as ordinary people,

981
00:58:08,247 --> 00:58:10,943
and when an order comes down, and then, bam!

982
00:58:10,943 --> 00:58:13,092
Just watch where you're going.

983
00:58:15,307 --> 00:58:18,491
After 15 years of all-out investigation
and still no arrest,

984
00:58:18,491 --> 00:58:23,626
maybe he's disguised himself
in a way we never imagined.

985
00:59:03,826 --> 00:59:09,043
Being in the field next to you
feels like a dream.

986
00:59:09,043 --> 00:59:11,692
I'm not here to make your dream come true.

987
00:59:11,692 --> 00:59:14,726
Next time, wish for something bigger.

988
00:59:15,792 --> 00:59:17,492
Okay.

989
00:59:22,187 --> 00:59:24,692
But why are you really here?

990
00:59:24,692 --> 00:59:27,659
I heard you don't personally
deal with White targets.

991
00:59:29,683 --> 00:59:32,592
Well, it just reminded me of the old days.

992
00:59:37,183 --> 00:59:41,299
Can I ask who your first client was?

993
00:59:41,299 --> 00:59:43,226
My first client...

994
00:59:47,295 --> 00:59:49,792
Well, who should I say it was?

995
00:59:50,663 --> 00:59:52,363
What?

996
00:59:57,259 --> 00:59:59,892
Okay, shall we go?

997
01:00:08,826 --> 01:00:11,259
Client meeting starts.

998
01:00:46,892 --> 01:00:49,699
So he was in the middle of
his working life, huh?

999
01:00:49,699 --> 01:00:52,563
<i>Darn it! Fell again!</i>

1000
01:00:52,563 --> 01:00:55,459
<i>Why do these things keep
crashing all the darn time?</i>

1001
01:00:57,111 --> 01:00:59,759
<i>Grip it tightly.</i>

1002
01:00:59,759 --> 01:01:02,359
<i>Otherwise, you'll break another bone.</i>

1003
01:01:05,126 --> 01:01:06,892
<i>Darn it!</i>

1004
01:01:09,351 --> 01:01:12,326
Oh, this is driving me crazy.

1005
01:01:24,439 --> 01:01:26,759
That punk...

1006
01:01:34,099 --> 01:01:35,743
Ms. Yoo, don't!

1007
01:01:35,743 --> 01:01:37,443
Ms. Oh Hyun Nam!

1008
01:01:59,759 --> 01:02:01,659
[Recording]

1009
01:02:01,659 --> 01:02:04,592
[Voice Recording File]

1010
01:02:06,159 --> 01:02:08,026
[Call Recording]

1011
01:02:08,026 --> 01:02:10,259
[June 27, 2018]

1012
01:02:11,792 --> 01:02:15,826
[June 27, 2018]

1013
01:02:33,159 --> 01:02:36,343
You fell because you have no patience,

1014
01:02:36,343 --> 01:02:40,292
yet people blame it all on me.

1015
01:02:41,359 --> 01:02:44,559
They just don't know how to raise tough kids.

1016
01:02:45,426 --> 01:02:47,959
What? Who are you?

1017
01:02:55,267 --> 01:02:57,081
<i>Someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor</i>

1018
01:02:57,081 --> 01:02:59,859
<i>of the emergency stairs at King Tower.</i>

1019
01:03:00,903 --> 01:03:03,611
<i>I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.</i>

1020
01:03:03,611 --> 01:03:08,692
<i>She could have witnessed Kingfisher
or been an accomplice.</i>

1021
01:03:15,855 --> 01:03:19,392
<i>Or she could even be Kingfisher herself.</i>

1022
01:04:43,135 --> 01:04:45,659
So you finally opened the door.

1023
01:04:45,659 --> 01:04:47,315
[Big Precious]
Tae Seong.

1024
01:04:47,315 --> 01:04:49,635
Stay together, or leave her...

1025
01:04:49,635 --> 01:04:52,131
I'm asking because I'm genuinely curious.

1026
01:04:52,131 --> 01:04:54,099
Give me an honest answer.

1027
01:04:54,099 --> 01:04:56,111
So an unavoidable variable
popped up with your husband.

1028
01:04:56,111 --> 01:04:57,659
If I leave for somewhere again...

1029
01:04:57,659 --> 01:04:58,659
Are you going somewhere?

1030
01:04:58,659 --> 01:05:00,392
It looks like our police network was hacked.

1031
01:05:00,392 --> 01:05:03,335
Could there be a Kingfisher operative
inside the police?

1032
01:05:03,335 --> 01:05:06,319
That woman who's your friend's wife...
What does she do for a living?

1033
01:05:06,319 --> 01:05:07,755
We've got a witness.

1034
01:05:07,755 --> 01:05:09,050
[Durumi Electronics]
Could Kingfisher

1035
01:05:09,050 --> 01:05:11,699
be a parent raising a child?

1036
01:05:11,699 --> 01:05:14,892
Is Kingfisher the person
you said you had to protect?

